---
title: "Step 3 · Review"
description: Book the period-end adjustments, review the manual changes, check the F5 and complete the quarter.
sidebar:
  order: 12
---

Step 3 has four tabs: **Period-end adjustments**, **Adjustment review**, **F5 check** and **Complete**. The small text under the step name shows how many quarter checks are not yet met.

## Period-end adjustments

The quarter-end items: foreign-currency revaluation, accruals, amortisation and similar items from the company's policies. The page shows which items are booked and which are not. From the same page, post an adjusting entry (**Post an adjusting entry**), record an **Asset disposal** or set up an **Instalment schedule**.

{% screenshot id="bookkeeping/review-period-end-adjustments" caption="Period-end adjustments: a foreign-currency revaluation not yet booked." /%}

## Adjustment review

Lists only the changes people made in this quarter and the entries Operon booked on its own. Review each one and select **Mark reviewed**. A manager's own change must be reviewed by another reviewer.

A red bar at the top of the page means that a books consistency check has failed. Select **Show** to see which check failed.

{% screenshot id="bookkeeping/review-adjustment-review" caption="Adjustment review, with the consistency bar at the top." /%}

## F5 check

The GST F5 boxes for this quarter, compared with the previous quarter. **Before filing**, on the right, lists what must be resolved before filing. While questions on the client query list are unanswered, the figures are marked **Provisional**.

When the figures are right, select **Confirm figures**. If the books change after confirmation, the F5 must be confirmed again.

{% screenshot id="bookkeeping/review-f5-check" caption="F5 check for Q3 2026." /%}

## Complete

The quarter checks, the control account balances and the bank reconciliation records. Each check that is not met has a **Resolve** button that goes to where it is fixed. The checks are:

- Every account and month is reconciled and signed off.
- The to-do list is clear (items on hold still count).
- No bank lines or statements are on hold.
- Nothing is waiting for the client.
- The suspense account is clear.
- The F5 is confirmed, and the books have not changed since.
- The manual changes are reviewed.
- No document is undetermined.

When every check is met, select **Complete quarter** at the bottom of the page. Completing locks the books of the quarter. To change the quarter again, a manager reopens it; see [Reopen a period](/en/bookkeeping/reopen/).

{% screenshot id="bookkeeping/review-complete" caption="Complete: the quarter checks." /%}

{% aside type="caution" title="Overriding a check" %}
If a check cannot be met but the quarter must be completed, only a manager can override the check, with a written reason. The override is recorded.
{% /aside %}
